WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
A hot summer day at the beach.

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:05.810
The sand and the sea
sit under the same Sun.

3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:10.060
By the afternoon, the sand is
too hot to stand on barefoot.

4
00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.120
The sea still feels cool.

5
00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.600
Same sunshine, all day long, on both.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.360
So why does the sand get so
much hotter than the sea?

7
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.620
In this mission, you'll calculate the
energy needed to warm a metal block,

8
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.560
or the water in a kettle.

9
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.590
Then you'll watch ice melt and water boil,

10
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.870
as the temperature stops rising
while energy keeps flowing in.

11
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: explain why the sand gets
scorching hot while the sea stays cool.
